"""Triton implementation of torch.einsum.

Architecture
------------
Host side parses the equation (ellipsis expansion, implicit output), builds a
label -> (dim, stride) map per operand (repeated labels collapse to a diagonal
via summed strides) and dispatches to one of three device kernels:

  * ``_gather_kernel``  - no contraction labels: pure permutation / diagonal /
    broadcast elementwise product (1 or 2 operands).
  * ``_reduce_kernel``  - single operand with summed labels (trace, full or
    dimension reductions), optionally split across programs.
  * ``_gemm_kernel``    - two operands with a non-empty contraction group,
    normalised to a batched GEMM over (batch, M, N, K) linearisations of the
    label groups.  ``tl.dot`` when the shapes allow, broadcast-FMA otherwise.

Multi-operand equations are contracted pairwise into freshly allocated
intermediates.  Every kernel addresses tensors through their real strides, so
no input copy or ``contiguous()`` is ever required.
"""

